; control_inplace_ry_reject_stateprep_step_cap_over.ll — DECLINE at N = 4200,
; just OVER F2's `kF2MaxSteps` fixpoint bound (`Truncated` => the loud F2
; string). The red half of the step-cap pin; the green half is
; `..._stateprep_step_cap_under.ll` (N = 4090).
;
; NOTE WHAT THE DECLINE STRING MEANS HERE. It is the SAME message an actual
; seed match prints, and that is deliberate (`Truncated` is folded into `Pinned`
; at the call site): a search that ran out of budget has not proved the region
; safe, so it must not read as an accept. The seed is 7 and nothing in the module
; folds to 7, so the ONLY thing being witnessed is the bound.
;
; ⚠ ROUND-4 RULE-13 FINDING (lens R4, F-R4-4, CONFIRMED-OVER-DECLINE — the SAFE
; direction, but UNPINNED). `kF2MaxSteps = 4096` bounds F2's forward fixpoint,
; and exceeding it sets `Truncated`, which DECLINES rather than accepting a
; search that stopped looking. R4 measured the boundary as reachable (1000 /
; 2000 / 4000 / 4090 users accept; 4200 / 8000 decline) and found NOTHING in the
; corpus pinning the constant: `grep 4096 ir-pass/test/*.ll` returned two files,
; one an unrelated `icmp ult %sh, 4096` in a PredMux fixture and one prose.
; Change the constant to 1024 or to 8192 and, before this pair, no test moved.
;
; THE PAIR. Both modules are the same program with a different chain length N:
; `%q` pinned to `{5}` on the arm edge, seed 7 (no fold of anything here is 7,
; so the ONLY reason either can decline is the step bound), and a linear chain of
; N tainted `add`s off `%q` — LINEAR because a 4000-wide FAN-OUT off one handle
; declines later at `uncompute: dead chain would free a measured register`
; (Rule 8), which would have made the accept side untestable.
;
; THE EXACT BOUNDARY, MEASURED 2026-09-05 rather than quoted: the walk pops `%q`
; and the tainted `icmp` (both anchors, both dominating the branch) plus the N
; chain members, so `Steps = N + 2`, and N=4094 ACCEPTS while N=4095 DECLINES —
; i.e. the cap is EXACTLY 4096. The shipped pair is deliberately LOOSER than
; that (4090 / 4200) so that a future change adding or removing one anchor does
; not redden a fixture for a reason unrelated to the constant; the tight figures
; are recorded here instead. File sizes are 129 KB / 133 KB and `cq-opt` costs
; 0.10 s / 0.08 s on them.
;
; ⚠ DO NOT "SIMPLIFY" THESE BY SHRINKING N. A pair that does not straddle the
; real constant pins nothing, which is the state R4 found.
;
; RUN: not %cq-opt -load-pass-plugin %cq-pass -passes=cq-lowering -S %s 2>&1 | %filecheck %s
; CHECK: error{{.*}}state prep seed is proven equal to the condition register under quantum control
; CHECK-NOT: cqrt_ry_i32_controlled

declare i32 @cq_theta_si32(i32, double)
declare i32 @cq_measure_si32(i32)

